<%# The tab icon, in one place for all three views (#688). Without a usable
    link a browser falls back to requesting /favicon.ico on every fresh page
    load, which fell through the static handler and all three routers to a 404.

    Two files rather than one: the SVG is what modern browsers pick and it
    scales to whatever the OS asks for, and the ICO is there because Safari
    reads no SVG icon at all — and a browser with no icon it can read is exactly
    the one that goes looking for /favicon.ico. Both are served out of public/,
    so the bare /favicon.ico request now resolves too.

    asset() stamps each URL with the file's content hash, so these get the same
    year-long immutable cache as the stylesheet and change when the icon does. %>
<link rel="icon" href="<%= asset('/favicon.ico') %>" sizes="32x32">
<link rel="icon" href="<%= asset('/favicon.svg') %>" type="image/svg+xml">
